    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "F2",
        "severity": "MEDIUM",
        "location": "vault.py:80-84",
        "requirement": "Valid transfers must succeed with existing benign triggers; valid CLI calls must exit 0.",
        "evidence": "Initialize a database and insert accounts ('one','a',100), ('one','b',0). Execute: CREATE TRIGGER begin AFTER INSERT ON audit BEGIN SELECT 1; END; Then call transfer(path,'one','a','b',10,'new'). SQLite accepts this harmless trigger, but the repaired implementation raises StopIteration at line 83 because line 81 mistakes its name for the trigger body delimiter. Independently reproduced through the API and CLI in DELETE and WAL modes: CLI exits 2 with empty stdout and a generic error; all data remains unchanged. The .pre-repair implementation succeeds with the identical trigger. Quoting the trigger name as \"begin\" also makes the current implementation succeed.",
        "suggested_fix": "Identify trigger events and body boundaries according to CREATE TRIGGER syntax, including SQLite's accepted keyword identifiers. Add API and CLI regression coverage for this valid unquoted trigger name."
      }
    ],
    "checks": [
      "Read CONTRACT.md, applicable instructions and lean-run write-integrity guidance; compared current application files against .baseline and .pre-repair and inspected added tests. The repair changes vault.py; app.py and test_regression.py are unchanged from .pre-repair.",
      "python3 -B -m unittest discover -v: all 24 tests passed.",
      "Independently reproduced the prior unique-index replacement defect in .pre-repair for audit, transfers and accounts. Current code rejects each destructive case with complete rollback in DELETE and WAL modes; matching OR IGNORE controls succeed. Schema definitions and foreign rows remain preserved, and historical replay after reopening makes no changes.",
      "Reviewed removal of foreign-account preservation lookups and captured SQL during public balance, transfer and replay calls. Stored account and receipt SELECTs were constrained to the authenticated tenant. Malformed foreign data and an ignored foreign-account collision did not disrupt the valid transfer.",
      "Verified benign nested IGNORE behavior, ignored deletes and harmless REPLACE with an existing DELETE failure trigger against .pre-repair.",
      "Confirmed F2 independently through API and subprocess CLI calls, including quoted-name controls. Used Python -B and temporary databases; no application, test, instruction or baseline files were modified."
    ],
    "coverage_limits": [
      "Executed on Python 3.14.3 and SQLite 3.50.4; other runtime versions were not tested.",
      "Review targeted the repair delta and contract regressions. Arbitrary SQLite trigger syntax and all possible trigger interactions were not exhaustively tested."
    ]
  },
